<h2 id="news-hook">NASA Lets You Read and Download Hundreds of Free E-Books</h2>

<p>NASA publishes a large, openly available e-book library, and it keeps growing coverage in 2026 as readers look for reliable, free EPUB sources that work on any device. The official <a href="https://www.nasa.gov/ebooks/" rel="noopener">NASA e-Books hub</a> invites you to "read and download free NASA e-Books on the agency&rsquo;s history, aeronautics research, science missions, and the International Space Station." Unlike most commercial ebook catalogs, NASA&rsquo;s titles are genuinely free, carry no DRM, and are offered in open formats you can move between devices without any conversion trick or jailbreak.</p>

<p>In late August 2026 the collection got fresh attention from the tech press, with outlets highlighting that you can pull down hundreds of free NASA titles and load them straight onto a Kindle, Kobo, or tablet. For anyone building a personal EPUB library, this is one of the best no-cost sources around &mdash; and one of the few major publishers to hand you <em>both</em> EPUB and PDF downloads directly on each book&rsquo;s page.</p>

<p>Here is what the NASA e-book library contains, how to download titles as EPUB, and how to get them onto the reader you already own.</p>

<h2 id="what-nasa-ebooks">What the NASA E-Book Library Includes</h2>

<p>NASA&rsquo;s e-book collection is organized into a few broad categories. On the main page you will find <strong>Aeronautics</strong>, <strong>NASA History</strong>, and <strong>Science</strong>, with the science section covering space missions, the Hubble Space Telescope, and the International Space Station. A rotating set of &ldquo;Featured&rdquo; titles highlights the most popular current books.</p>

<p>Notable, freely downloadable titles include <em>Hubble&rsquo;s Beautiful Universe</em>, <em>Hubble Science Highlights</em>, <em>Hubble: An Overview of the Space Telescope</em>, and the <em>Hubble Focus</em> series covering gravitational lenses, black holes, the dark universe, strange new worlds, and the lives of stars. The history side carries year-by-year accounts from the Apollo era through the Shuttle program, and the aeronautics section covers NASA&rsquo;s contributions to flight research.</p>

<p>Because these are official NASA releases, the photography and diagrams are unusually high quality for free e-books &mdash; full-resolution telescope imagery and mission illustrations that look excellent on a color e-reader or tablet screen.</p>

<h2 id="formats">EPUB, PDF, or Both: What NASA Hands You</h2>

<p>The strongest reason to use NASA&rsquo;s library is the file format. On each individual e-book page, NASA lists separate <strong>PDF</strong> and <strong>EPUB</strong> download buttons with the file size and date. For example, the Hubble &ldquo;Beautiful Universe&rdquo; volume offers a PDF download and a separate EPUB download, both updated in 2025 and both completely free.</p>

